    "instructions": "Fiber AI API - Discovery and execution tools.\n\nHOW TO USE (3 steps):\n1. search_endpoints(\"your intent\", constraints=[...], preferredTags=[...], tagPack=\"...\") - Choose the best operations with ranked alternatives\n2. get_endpoint_details_full(\"operationId\") - Get complete schema and examples for complex fields\n3. call_operation(\"operationId\", {body: {...}}) - Execute\n\nEXAMPLES:\n- \"find companies\" → search_endpoints(\"find AI companies in SF\", constraints=[\"country\", \"headcount\"]) → companySearch\n- \"get email\" → search_endpoints(\"reveal work email for known profile\") → syncContactEnrichment\n- \"find people\" → search_endpoints(\"find VP engineering in fintech\") → peopleSearch\n\nAUTHENTICATION: Every API call requires an apiKey parameter. Ask the user for their Fiber API key (starts with sk_live_ or sk_test_) and include it in every call_operation request body.\n\nFOR COMPLEX WORKFLOWS (bulk operations, audiences):\nRead llms://fiber.ai/llms.txt for step-by-step guidance.\nFor API choice among similar operations, read llms://fiber.ai/api-selector.\n",
